{"base_rate":0.4709066305818674,"brier":0.21090771312584572,"bss":0.1535031660640268,"bss_hi":0.24742634095745894,"bss_lo":0.047510453107882794,"chart":{"base":[672.6,69.4],"fp":[384.3,337.2],"lead":"62,210.7 272,177.8 482,153.5 692,66.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.15 — higher than 23% of cities","fp":"low end +18pp, high end +7pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 15% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 5%; promised 94% → rained 82%"},"rel":"62,443.4 81.1,338.6 181.3,267.3 416.5,166.5 652.4,112.3"},"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.17063599458728007,"ess":541.4156236395876,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Montreal</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Montreal rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 739 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMONTRéAL 2.6 SSW, 0.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.15, ranked 164 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(128&ndash;182) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>134</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Montreal</b> <span class=\"muted\">Canada</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.15</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>128&ndash;182\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>739 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Montreal &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p