lass=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"100.34384615384614\" cy=\"274.66666666666663\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 26%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"151.76083333333332\" cy=\"149.44444444444446\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 65% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"217.11610389610394\" cy=\"145.63636363636363\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 68%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"299.49589041095896\" cy=\"112.7397260273973\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 81% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"369.95643835616437\" cy=\"87.8082191780822\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"408.7394736842105\" cy=\"80.26315789473682\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(47%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Montreal the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.44).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>65%</td><td class='num'>-0.440</td><td class='num'>35.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>212</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.180</td><td class='num'>12.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.285</td><td class='num'>7.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.376</td><td class='num'>9.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":45.50884,"lon":-73.58781,"n":739,"n_cities":213,"name":"Montreal","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":134,"obs":0.05223880597014925,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.013648648648648648,"n":74,"obs":0.24324324324324326,"sig":true},{"hi":0.07,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.04524390243902438,"n":82,"obs":0.34146341463414637,"sig":true},{"hi":0.19,"lo":0.07,"mean":0.1196153846153846,"n":78,"obs":0.2948717948717949,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.19,"mean":0.2648611111111111,"n":72,"obs":0.6388888888888888,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5660000000000002,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.4494805194805196,"n":77,"obs":0.6493506493506493,"sig":true},{"hi":0.81,"lo":0.5